= Public-key cryptography — Simple =

Public-key cryptography uses a pair of related keys. One can be public; the other must remain private. Different schemes use the pair for encryption, digital signatures, or establishing shared secrets.

'''Important boundary:''' public-key cryptography ≠ encryption only.

